<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for March 5.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for March 5.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas consumption for the period March 3-5.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 3 (actual) 285 mcm, 67 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 4 (forecast) 284 mcm, 66 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 5 (forecast) 295 mcm, 69 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 3 (actual) 6.0 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.4 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 4 (forecast) 8.5 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.4 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 5 (forecast) 7.4 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.5 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption on Tuesday and TransCo says the probability of interruption on Wednesday was low.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
